  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466490",
      "title": "Getting Started with Feature Modules",
      "lectureOrder": 648,
      "videoOrder": 596,
      "sourceHash": "71c980afed70424b1c065218d5b4013dcc19a905a0592d48ed2f49495c47de48",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.28,
          "end": 4.83,
          "en": "Instructor: So we can work with multiple modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.83,
          "end": 8.58,
          "en": "instead of having one big AppModule, we could split",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.58,
          "end": 11.85,
          "en": "that into an AppModule that defines our AppComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.85,
          "end": 14.19,
          "en": "And then we have in this slide here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.19,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "two separate new modules, so called Feature Modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 20.79,
          "en": "Now, the term Feature Module does not mean",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.79,
          "end": 22.65,
          "en": "that you create them in a special way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.65,
          "end": 26.82,
          "en": "It's still a class with the appNgModule decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.82,
          "end": 29.76,
          "en": "It just means that this is a module that groups",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.76,
          "end": 33.84,
          "en": "together components, directives, pipes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.84,
          "end": 38.84,
          "en": "that are used in a certain feature area of your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.91,
          "end": 40.86,
          "en": "Like in this slide, when we're building,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.86,
          "end": 42.3,
          "en": "let's say an online shop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.3,
          "end": 45.69,
          "en": "we could have components that are primarily involved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.69,
          "end": 49.14,
          "en": "in rendering products and individual products",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.14,
          "end": 52.35,
          "en": "and we could outsource those into a ProductsModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 54.87,
          "en": "And if we then have an area in our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.87,
          "end": 57.63,
          "en": "where we're primarily concerned with orders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.63,
          "end": 62.63,
          "en": "then we could also outsource that into our OrdersModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.64,
          "end": 65.91,
          "en": "Now that is an important step of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.91,
          "end": 68.16,
          "en": "Angular application development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.16,
          "end": 70.74,
          "en": "splitting your app into such feature modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.74,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "because that is the prerequisite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "to performance improvements, we'll dive into later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 78.63,
          "en": "And that also now ensures that when our developers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.63,
          "end": 81.45,
          "en": "work on your code or you work on your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.45,
          "end": 84.99,
          "en": "maybe after a short pause you quickly know where to look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.99,
          "end": 89.19,
          "en": "for the setup for this specific part of your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.19,
          "end": 91.83,
          "en": "Because of course, you could be building an application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.83,
          "end": 94.86,
          "en": "with hundreds or thousands of components and directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.86,
          "end": 98.78999999999999,
          "en": "and then grouping them together into logical modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 101.49000000000001,
          "en": "makes working with them and refactoring your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 102.93,
          "en": "simply much easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 105.9,
          "en": "Now let's apply that to our course project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.9,
          "end": 109.17,
          "en": "where we also have multiple features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.17,
          "end": 113.78999999999999,
          "en": "Which features do we have in our course project there?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 118.22999999999999,
          "en": "Well, we, if we have a look at it in our app folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.22999999999999,
          "end": 121.89,
          "en": "I'd say we have free main feature areas.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.89,
          "end": 124.5,
          "en": "We have the recipes feature area,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.5,
          "end": 127.17,
          "en": "so all the components related to recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.17,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "We have the shopping list feature area,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 131.79,
          "en": "with all the logic related to the shopping list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "And we have the auth feature area,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "where we have all the components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 138.12,
          "en": "and all the logic related to authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.12,
          "end": 140.01,
          "en": "Even if in this case it's only one component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.01,
          "end": 142.53,
          "en": "but still it's a separate feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 145.26,
          "en": "The header and the shared components here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.26,
          "end": 148.5,
          "en": "I'd say these are not really features of the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 148.5,
          "end": 151.05,
          "en": "the header is part of the AppComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 151.05,
          "end": 153.75,
          "en": "We do render it there so it definitely belongs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 153.75,
          "end": 156.42000000000002,
          "en": "to the root of our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.42000000000002,
          "end": 158.76,
          "en": "And regarding the shared components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.76,
          "end": 161.97,
          "en": "in this app we might only use certain features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.97,
          "end": 163.47,
          "en": "in certain parts of the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.47,
          "end": 164.79,
          "en": "Let's say the alert component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.79,
          "end": 166.82999999999998,
          "en": "we only use it in the auth component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 166.82999999999998,
          "end": 168.96,
          "en": "but it would make sense that we share that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 168.96,
          "end": 172.2,
          "en": "across different features of our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.2,
          "end": 173.54,
          "en": "because you could be showing an alert",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 173.54,
          "end": 177.21,
          "en": "in the recipes area as well when you fail to load recipes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.21,
          "end": 180.36,
          "en": "So the alert and so on, these shared things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.36,
          "end": 181.65,
          "en": "we'll take care about later,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 181.65,
          "end": 184.86,
          "en": "they're not really a feature module of this app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.86,
          "end": 188.58,
          "en": "But let's dive into creating a module for our recipe then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.58,
          "end": 190.62,
          "en": "And for this, in the recipes folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 190.62,
          "end": 192.99,
          "en": "you simply create a new TypeScript file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 192.99,
          "end": 196.5,
          "en": "and you would name this recipes.module.ts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 196.5,
          "end": 200.25,
          "en": "just as we have the appmodule for our general application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 200.25,
          "end": 203.31,
          "en": "So basically the core setup for the entire app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 203.31,
          "end": 206.85,
          "en": "We now have the recipes module that should be responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 206.85,
          "end": 211.38,
          "en": "for defining the building blocks of the recipe feature area.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 211.38,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "And for that, you simply export a class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 215.88,
          "en": "and name it RecipesModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 215.88,
          "end": 217.47,
          "en": "that is the naming convention here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 217.47,
          "end": 219.39,
          "en": "Just as you named the RecipesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 219.39,
          "end": 220.98,
          "en": "well, RecipesComponent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 220.98,
          "end": 224.013,
          "en": "You now name the recipes module, RecipesModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 224.97,
          "end": 227.43,
          "en": "This class now needs a decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 227.43,
          "end": 230.85,
          "en": "and you can probably guess which decorator that is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 230.85,
          "end": 234.36,
          "en": "it is the NgModule decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 234.36,
          "end": 237.69299999999998,
          "en": "NgModule is imported from @angularcore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 238.632,
          "end": 241.08,
          "en": "Now the NgModule decorator takes a object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 241.08,
          "end": 243.57,
          "en": "which you pass in, to configure that module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 243.57,
          "end": 245.88,
          "en": "and there you now can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 245.88,
          "end": 249.81,
          "en": "basically whatever you also added to the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 249.81,
          "end": 253.32,
          "en": "So since we're talking about the RecipesModule here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 253.32,
          "end": 255.81,
          "en": "we, for example, will a add declarations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.81,
          "end": 259.53,
          "en": "and add all recipes related components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.53,
          "end": 261.75,
          "en": "to this RecipesModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 261.75,
          "end": 263.64,
          "en": "So if we have a look at the AppModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 263.64,
          "end": 265.149,
          "en": "we got the RecipesComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 265.149,
          "end": 267.99,
          "en": "the RecipeList and Detail, and RecipeItemComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 267.99,
          "end": 271.65,
          "en": "and also the RecipeStart and EditComponents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 271.65,
          "end": 274.68,
          "en": "All these components, I'll remove them here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 274.68,
          "end": 276.81,
          "en": "from the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 276.81,
          "end": 281.13,
          "en": "and move them into declarations of my RecipesModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 281.13,
          "end": 284.733,
          "en": "So let's wrap these here as well, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 287.34000000000003,
          "end": 288.78,
          "en": "That should be it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 288.78,
          "end": 292.68,
          "en": "Let's remove the line breaks here in the appmodule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 292.68,
          "end": 295.02,
          "en": "And of course in the appmodule we can now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 295.02,
          "end": 298.86,
          "en": "all remove the unused import statements here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 298.86,
          "end": 301.32,
          "en": "of all these recipe related components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 301.32,
          "end": 303.9,
          "en": "because we don't need to import the types",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.9,
          "end": 305.94,
          "en": "into this AppModule file anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 305.94,
          "end": 307.71,
          "en": "if we're not using them here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 307.71,
          "end": 309.39,
          "en": "And now therefore, in the recipes module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 309.39,
          "end": 311.16,
          "en": "we need to add the imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 311.16,
          "end": 313.68,
          "en": "And here the IDE might be able to help you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 313.68,
          "end": 315.72,
          "en": "if you get something like a light bulb, here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 315.72,
          "end": 318.06,
          "en": "You can simply let the IDE import this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 318.06,
          "end": 320.49,
          "en": "Otherwise simply add these import statements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 320.49,
          "end": 323.55,
          "en": "with the correct paths on your own, of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 323.55,
          "end": 327.093,
          "en": "So I'll quickly add them all with the help of my IDE here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 330.18,
          "end": 333.9,
          "en": "Can also use all missing imports.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 333.9,
          "end": 336.57,
          "en": "And now we made a first important step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 336.57,
          "end": 340.62,
          "en": "towards our RecipesModule, but actually not one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 340.62,
          "end": 343.14300000000003,
          "en": "that will suffice, not at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 344.4,
          "end": 348.027,
          "en": "How can we now use our RecipesModule in the AppModule?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 351.21,
          "end": 353.25,
          "en": "Now, as a first step, since I declare",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 353.25,
          "end": 356.67,
          "en": "all the recipe components here, we could simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 356.67,
          "end": 360.24,
          "en": "add the exports array to the recipes module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 360.24,
          "end": 364.68,
          "en": "and export all components which we declared here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 364.68,
          "end": 367.41,
          "en": "so that we can not just use them in the recipes module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 367.41,
          "end": 371.16,
          "en": "but in any module that imports the recipe module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 371.16,
          "end": 373.14,
          "en": "And that could be the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 373.14,
          "end": 375.45,
          "en": "So here, now, I cleaned up the declarations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 375.45,
          "end": 377.19,
          "en": "to kind of bring them back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 377.19,
          "end": 379.35,
          "en": "They are now declared in the recipes module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 379.35,
          "end": 382.77,
          "en": "we now have to import the recipes module here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 382.77,
          "end": 384.78,
          "en": "So simply add recipes module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 384.78,
          "end": 387.3,
          "en": "to the imports of the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 387.3,
          "end": 389.22,
          "en": "And of course make sure you also add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 389.22,
